           "source_section": "Definition",
-          "quote": "Let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be the open trial-initial-state set, and assume $B$ is $C^1$ on the required endpoint pairs, meaning it is totally differentiable with continuous derivative entries. Inputs are a certified evaluator from [[def-certified-ivp-approximation-and-sensitivity-interface]] that succeeds on each queried trial, an initial value $s_0\\in U$, residual tolerance $\\tau\\ge0$, and a correction budget $M\\in\\mathbb N_0$. Form the computed residual $\\widetilde R(s)=B(s,\\widetilde\\Phi(s))$ and its exact derivative for that numerical residual using [[prop-shooting-residual-derivative]]. For $k=0,1,\\ldots,M$, in this order:\n\n1. Evaluate $\\widetilde R(s_k)$ and $D\\widetilde R(s_k)$. If evaluation fails, return the last valid state with status evaluator-failure and no residual certificate.\n2. If $\\|\\widetilde R(s_k)\\|_2\\le\\tau$, return $s_k$, its approximate trajectory, and status root-tolerance-met. This status asserts only the displayed residual tolerance.\n3. If $k=M$, return the last state and status iteration-budget-exhausted.\n4. Call [[alg-newton-correction-for-vector-residuals]] with $A=D\\widetilde R(s_k)$ and $r=\\widetilde R(s_k)$. If it reports singular-jacobian, stop with that status.\n5. If the proposed state $s_k+u_k$ is outside $U$, return the last state with status invalid-trial; otherwise set $s_{k+1}=s_k+u_k$.\n\nThis is the finite-budget Newton procedure guarded by the evaluator's failure status. On a sequence of successful evaluations it has the same residual, singularity, domain and budget checks as [[alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals]]. It makes no global-start, exact-root, or discretization-error claim.\n",
+          "quote": "Let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be the open trial-initial-state set. Let $D_B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d\\times\\mathbb R^d$ be the open domain of the $C^1$ boundary map $B$, where $C^1$ means total differentiability with continuous derivative entries. Inputs are a certified evaluator from [[def-certified-ivp-approximation-and-sensitivity-interface]], an initial trial $s_0\\in U$, residual tolerance $\\tau\\ge0$, and a correction budget $M\\in\\mathbb N_0$. The evaluator may return failure on a queried trial. Every successful response must supply the approximate trajectory, the endpoint $\\widetilde\\Phi(s)$ and the exact derivative $D\\widetilde\\Phi(s)$ of the declared $C^1$ numerical endpoint map, with the interface's stated uniform trajectory-error bound. Success on every queried trial is not an input assumption.\n\nFor $k=0,1,\\ldots,M$, in this order:\n\n1. Query the evaluator at $s_k$. If it fails, return the last accepted trial with status evaluator-failure and no residual certificate. Before evaluating $B$, check $(s_k,\\widetilde\\Phi(s_k))\\in D_B$; if this fails or cannot be established, return the last accepted trial with status invalid-endpoint-pair and no residual certificate. On success form $\\widetilde R(s_k)=B(s_k,\\widetilde\\Phi(s_k))$ and $D\\widetilde R(s_k)=D_1B(s_k,\\widetilde\\Phi(s_k))+D_2B(s_k,\\widetilde\\Phi(s_k))D\\widetilde\\Phi(s_k)$ using [[prop-shooting-residual-derivative]]. A failure to evaluate these quantities returns evaluator-failure without a residual certificate.\n2. If $\\|\\widetilde R(s_k)\\|_2\\le\\tau$, return $s_k$, its approximate trajectory, and status root-tolerance-met. This status asserts only the displayed residual tolerance.\n3. If $k=M$, return the last trial and status iteration-budget-exhausted.\n4. Call [[alg-newton-correction-for-vector-residuals]] with $A=D\\widetilde R(s_k)$ and $r=\\widetilde R(s_k)$. If it reports singular-jacobian, stop with that status.\n5. If the proposed trial $s_k+u_k$ is outside $U$ or its membership cannot be established, return the last accepted trial with status invalid-trial; otherwise accept $s_{k+1}=s_k+u_k$. Initially the last accepted trial is $s_0$; accepting a trial supplies no boundary residual certificate until step 1 succeeds there.\n\nOn a sequence of successful evaluations with endpoint pairs in $D_B$, this has the same residual, singularity, trial-domain and budget checks as [[alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals]]. It makes no global-start, exact-root, or discretization-error claim. The numerical residual is $C^1$ on the open subset of $U$ where $(s,\\widetilde\\Phi(s))\\in D_B$; no boundary value is evaluated outside that subset.",
           "uses": [
             "2.1"
           ]
