ed differentiable segment evaluators satisfying the same interface, or run [[alg-midpoint-collocation-for-nonlinear-bvps]] using the pointwise field/boundary values and their exact derivatives required by its residual. Use the residuals of [[def-phase-bordered-multiple-shooting-and-midpoint-collocation]]; in section mode include the constant parameter and affine section row. Missing pointwise/segment evaluation data returns evaluator-unavailable. Use the last finite tuple's first physical state and positive period (and parameter in section mode) as a shooting candidate. Reject a candidate outside $Z$ or a nonrational candidate without a supplied rational proposal; rationalization is only a new candidate, not a trajectory or residual certificate.\n\nAll modes propagate evaluator-failure, invalid-endpoint-pair, invalid-trial, singular-jacobian, inconclusive and exhausted-budget statuses. No candidate mode is assumed to succeed from arbitrary data. In particular, the first mode composes the available interval-enclosure provider directly; it does not infer a $C^1$ point evaluator from interval boxes.\n\n**Independent validation:** run [[alg-krawczyk-root-certification]] on $F$ and $Z$ with $C,W,\\eta$ and the supplied box budget. First its exact check $WC=I$ must succeed. For every processed subbox $Y\\subseteq Z$, let $m_Y$ be its rational midpoint. The residual callback runs the validated shooting jet on $\\{m_Y\\}$ and returns its $F(m_Y)$ enclosure as $F_0$; the Jacobian callback runs it on $Y$ and returns its $DF(Y)$ enclosure as $J(Y)$. Both append the sound outward section-row enclosures in section mode. This uses the actual midpoint of the current Krawczyk box, even when it differs from the candidate center. A failed query or tube inclusion marks that box unresolved. All interval operations are outward under [[lem-real-interval-arithmetic-preserves-enclosure]]. Retain only a box $Y$ with strict Krawczyk inclusion and its separately certified contraction bound be